   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Tesla coil. Members of the Tesla Coil Builders Association seen with their largest coil, nicknamed 'Nemesis'. A Tesla coil is essentially a large air-core transformer with a capacitor, named after its inventor, physicist Nikola Tesla (1856-1943). The coil is designed to give a high-voltage, high- frequency spark. 'Nemesis' creates a spark sixty times per second using mains electricity, but at over 1 million volts. Photographed in Richmond, Virginia, USA. </rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
