   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">17 Apr 1947, New York, New York, USA --- New York: Anita Howarth is shown removing a well cooked hamburger sandwich, fifteen seconds after it was placed in the new Raytheon Radarange, during a demonstration today at the engineering societies auditorium in New York City. The new machine, as easy to operate as an ordinary electric range, utilizes the Raytheon Magnetron, the very heart of radar, from which radio frequency energy waves are concentrated directly into the "oven." This amazing new machine can cook a half of a small sized fresh chicken in 4 minutes and a frankfurter in ten seconds. --- Image by Â© Bettmann/CORBIS</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <dc:title>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">U1062834INP</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:title>
   <dc:rights>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Â© Corbis.  All Rights Reserved.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:rights>
